{%- comment -%}
  product-img — a compatibility shim for the SEARCH APP, not theme vocabulary.

  DO NOT USE THIS IN v3 SECTIONS. The theme's own product tile is
  `snippets/product-card.liquid`; this exists for one reason only.

  WHY IT EXISTS
  The header's search box goes to /a/search — an APP PROXY served by the
  cloud-search app, not by templates/search.json. The app returns Liquid that
  Shopify renders inside the theme, and that Liquid calls
  `{% render 'product-img' %}`, a snippet the old T4S theme provided. On v3 it
  did not exist, so every result on the page printed:

      Liquid error (line 353): Could not find asset snippets/product-img.liquid

  Reported 02/09/2026, one line per result, with the images missing entirely.

  WHAT CHANGED FROM LIVE'S VERSION
  Live's is T4S: `t4s-product-img`, `lazyloadt4s`, `data-src`/`data-widths`
  driven by the lazysizes library, and a `lazyloadt4s-loader` span. None of
  that exists in v3 — there is no lazysizes, and the t4s classes have no rules
  behind them. So this renders a plain responsive <img> with native lazy
  loading and keeps only the interface the app depends on:

      image     the image object (required)
      eager     load immediately — the app passes this for the first row
      lcp       high fetch priority for the single top-left image
      imgatt    extra attributes the app injects on the wrapper

  The aspect-ratio custom property is kept because the app's own stylesheet
  reads it to size the cell before the image lands.

  IF THE APP EVER STOPS CALLING THIS, delete it. It is dead weight otherwise.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign img_eager = eager | default: false
  assign img_lcp = lcp | default: false
  assign img_loading = 'lazy'
  if img_eager
    assign img_loading = 'eager'
  endif
  assign img_alt = image.alt | default: ''
-%}
<div class="pimg" {{ imgatt }} style="--aspect-ratioapt: {{ image.aspect_ratio | default: 1 }}">
  {{ image | image_url: width: 600 | image_tag:
     loading: img_loading,
     fetchpriority: img_lcp | default: 'auto',
     widths: '180, 220, 280, 360, 440, 600',
     sizes: '(max-width: 560px) 50vw, (max-width: 900px) 33vw, 240px',
     alt: img_alt,
     class: 'pimg__img' }}
</div>

{%- comment -%}
  Styling lives here rather than in fye-core because this is app scaffolding,
  not part of the design system. A snippet cannot carry {% stylesheet %}, so
  the two rules it genuinely needs are inline on the elements above and here:
  square ratio and cover. Anything more would be styling the app's page, which
  is a separate decision — see the note in build-state about whether search
  should be the app proxy or the theme's own /search page at all.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  .pimg { position: relative; overflow: hidden; }
  .pimg__img { display: block; width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 1; object-fit: cover; }
</style>
